# LLM Assist — editor selection contract

The **「선택된 텍스트」** field in `LlmAssistPanel` must stay in sync with the active markdown editor, including after focus moves to the LLM panel / dock / popout chrome.

## Single source of truth

| Layer | Module | Responsibility |
|-------|--------|----------------|
| Read / replace | `src/utils/editorSelection.ts` | `getEditorSelectionFromRef`, `subscribeEditorSelectionFromRef`, `applyLlmResultToEditor` |
| Focus memory | `src/utils/mdEditorSourceFocus.ts` | Last source-Editor caret/selection while CM had focus |
| Host state | `src/components/llm/LlmAssistModal.tsx` | `selectedText`, `refreshSelection`, subscription lifecycle |
| Bridge | `MarkdownEditor.jsx` + `LlmAssistSessionContext` | `registerEditorBridge({ editorRef, onChange, getMarkdown })` for the active file |

Do **not** read CodeMirror selection inline in panel/modal code. Always go through `editorSelection.ts`.

## Read order (`getEditorSelectionFromRef`)

1. **Live CodeMirror range** when `sliceString(from, to)` is non-empty.
2. **`getMdEditorSourceFocus(view)`** when live selection is collapsed but focus history has `from !== to`.
3. **`api.getSelectedText()`** as last resort (view missing or md-editor API still has text).
4. Apply / replace still uses focus memory via `applyLlmResultToEditor` — keep read + apply aligned.

## Host wiring checklist

1. Active `MarkdownEditor` registers `registerEditorBridge` when `isActiveFile && !previewOnly`.
2. `AppLayout` must pass `isActiveFile` into `editorPaneProps` (keep-alive tabs).
3. Bridge includes `getEditorApi()` — do not read `editorRef.current?.value` blindly.
4. `LlmAssistModal` resolves `editorRef` from `session.editorBridge` (not a stale local ref).
5. On open / bridge change → `refreshSelection()`; while open → `subscribeEditorSelectionFromRef` + polling fallback.
6. Docked mode must not leave `hidden=true` from floating minimize (blocks selection sync).
7. `refreshSelection` must **not** clear `selectedText` when `editorRef` is temporarily missing.
8. Popout sync includes `selectedText` + `selectionRange` from the same helpers.

## Subscription implementation

`subscribeEditorSelectionFromRef` must attach CodeMirror listeners with **`StateEffect.appendConfig.of(compartment.of(...))`** on first attach, then `compartment.reconfigure(...)` on later updates. Never call `reconfigure` on a compartment that is not yet in editor state.

## Tests required when touching this area

Update `tests/utils/editorSelection.test.ts` (and `mdEditorSourceFocus.test.ts` if apply behavior changes):

- live CM selection
- collapsed live selection + focus-history fallback
- live selection preferred over stale focus history
- `getSelectedText` fallback
- subscribe retry until view mounts

```text
❌ BAD — LlmAssistModal reads editorRef.current.getEditorView() directly
❌ BAD — refreshSelection clears selectedText when editorBridge is briefly null
❌ BAD — getEditorSelectionFromRef ignores mdEditorSourceFocus (breaks after panel focus)
❌ BAD — selection listener uses compartment.reconfigure without appendConfig first
✅ GOOD — getEditorSelectionFromRef + subscribeEditorSelectionFromRef + tests
✅ GOOD — MarkdownEditor keeps attachMdEditorSourceFocusTracking on the source view
✅ GOOD — registerEditorBridge only for active, non-preview editor tab
```

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.

## Streaming (`onChunk` contract)

All LLM transform clients (`geminiClient`, `openaiCompatibleClient`, `mlxVlmRuntime`) must call `onChunk` with **accumulated** output text, never a bare delta.

| Provider | Accumulation site |
|----------|-------------------|
| Gemini / OpenAI compatible | client (`accumulated += delta` before `onChunk`) |
| MLX-VLM worker | `mlx_vlm_generate_worker.py` (`accumulated += segment`) |
| MLX-VLM bridge | `mergeMlxVlmStreamChunk` in `mlxVlmRuntime.ts` (defense in depth) |

`LlmAssistModal` passes `setResult` directly to `onChunk` — do not append again in the panel.

When adding a new streaming provider, add a unit test that multi-chunk output grows monotonically.

```text
❌ BAD — onChunk(delta) while UI does setResult(chunk)
❌ BAD — worker emits chunk.text = latest token only without accumulation
✅ GOOD — onChunk(accumulated); UI setResult(accumulated)
✅ GOOD — mergeMlxVlmStreamChunk test for delta + accumulated payloads
```
